      "side": 1,
      "message": "Per discussion: we should probably track the lifetime somewhere. Options include:\n- A new class that contains an IpPrefix and has expiry times like LinkAddress\n- Add expiry times to IpPrefix itself\n\nI\u0027m not sure if the lifetimes really belong in IpPrefix. A prefix is just a group of addresses. It does not inherently have a lifetime, and often it\u0027s not associated with any lifetimes (e.g., when it\u0027s in a RouteInfo object - even if the route has an expiry because it comes from autoconf, it\u0027s not the prefix that expires, it\u0027s the route).\n\nOTOH, there are at least two use cases for prefixes: SLAAC (on-link prefix) and DHCPv6 PD (delegated prefix). It would be good to use the same class for both these cases, but what should that class be called? AssignedPrefix? ConfiguredPrefix? LinkPrefix, for consistency with LinkAddress? PrefixConfiguration? PrefixWithLifetime?\n\nAssignedPrefix would be a good term for cases like cellular networks which assign the whole prefix to the device, but do not \"delegate\" the prefix using prefix delegation...",
      "revId": "d2d68caf6c35e73948a621d5e1dfc5e8306c2d87",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
